  "commit_sha": "6378192a0ab4118bf87d880b869ef22d2617c59c",
  "corpus_role": "extraction_development_corpus",
  "corpus_role_detail": "The twenty source documents in this corpus were inspected to diagnose HTML structure while the SEC Item heading parser was developed. Extraction results over them are IN-SAMPLE DEVELOPMENT results and are not evidence that extraction generalizes to unseen filings. A separately frozen holdout corpus, selected only after the extraction parser is frozen, is required for that.",
  "determinism_check": "build run twice on identical inputs; build_hash and every bounded field identical across runs",
  "deterministic": true,
  "extraction_holdout_evaluation": false,
  "extraction_parser_developed_using_this_corpus": true,
  "filing_extraction_outcomes": {
    "extracted": 20
  },
  "generalization_claim_supported": false,
  "manifest_hash": "d630773f9d69ebba833158f86147b9749b09a98772454994357cd1893a1d6ac0",
  "manifest_status": "source_verified",
  "notes": [
    "IN-SAMPLE DEVELOPMENT RESULT. The twenty source documents in this corpus were inspected to diagnose HTML structure while sec_html_item_headings.v2 was designed, so 20/20 extraction measures the parser's fit to documents it was built against. It is NOT a holdout result and NOT evidence of generalization. A separately frozen holdout corpus, selected only after extraction v2 is frozen, is required before any generalization claim.",
    "Item 1A now extracts for all 20 sides. The v1 report in this directory records the prior 0-of-20 result and is preserved unchanged as the null-extraction baseline.",
    "Root cause of the v1 null result: real EDGAR 10-K HTML carries no <h1>-<h6> elements, and the HTML loader derived section_title from heading tags only. Item headings are styled div/span/p/table-cell blocks.",
    "The fix is generic SEC Item heading recognition (loaders/sec_headings.py, sec_html_item_headings.v2): a closed Item grammar over browser-faithful normalized visible text, plus deterministic contents/navigation disambiguation. No issuer, accession, filename, or hash rule exists, and no text was copied from any benchmark filing.",
    "The source corpus is unchanged: same manifest, same twenty filings, same twenty source sha256 digests, same issuer slate. No pair was replaced.",
    "The detector, heading alignment, validators, governance thresholds, and retry/lease/worker behavior were NOT modified. Extraction was not tuned after observing detector output.",
    "Unit counts are coarse for most filings: the detector's risk-factor heading pattern requires a heading ending in 'Risk'/'Risks', which most real filings do not use, so those sections reduce to a single preamble unit. That is a detector limitation recorded honestly here, not an extraction failure, and it is out of scope for this change.",
    "NO ACCURACY CLAIM. Zero labels are human_verified, so no gold metric exists for any pair.",
    "Extracted section text is written only under gitignored benchmark_data/."
  ],
